  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "The Shader class serves as the core GPU resource manager, handling the entire lifecycle of WebGL shaders. It asynchronously loads GLSL source code, processes modular includes via SHADER_FUNCTIONS, compiles, and links vertex/fragment shaders into a usable WebGLProgram. It manages geometry data by creating and binding WebGLBuffers derived from MeshData, and provides extensive methods for setting uniforms and managing rendering state."
  },
